Project Testing – Markdown Words

Project Testing – Checking whether the project works correctly and meets requirements.

Test Case – A set of steps used to check a specific function.

Unit Testing – Testing individual modules or components.

Integration Testing – Testing combined modules to ensure they work together.

System Testing – Testing the complete system.

Functional Testing – Checking whether all required functions work properly.

Performance Testing – Checking speed, stability, and responsiveness.

User Acceptance Testing (UAT) – Checking whether the system meets user needs.

Bug – An error or problem in the software.

Debugging – Finding and fixing bugs.

Validation – Checking whether the project meets the requirements.

Test Report – Recording the results and issues found during testing.

